        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John David McPhun\n- Places: Salisbury, Rhodesia, Harare, Southern Rhodesia\n- Roles: first-class cricketer\n- Organizations: Rhodesia cricket team\n- Events: Currie Cup\n- Concepts: de facto successor state, responsible government\n\nFacts:\n- Southern Rhodesia achieved responsible government in 1923.\n- Rhodesia had its capital in Salisbury, which is now called Harare.\n- Rhodesia was considered a de facto successor state to the former British colony of Southern Rhodesia.\n- John David McPhun was born on September 8, 1940, in Salisbury, Rhodesia.\n- John David McPhun was a first-class cricketer who played for Rhodesia in the Currie Cup.",
